, they are green. Harry is green and smart, so he must be white. But Harry is green, which is a different color. Wait, rule 10 says if someone is smart and white, then they are green. It doesn't say that being green and smart implies being white. So Harry being green and smart doesn't necessarily mean he's white. However, from rule 14, if someone is red and green, they are big. Harry is green but not necessarily red, so we can't conclude he's big unless more info is given.\n\nWait, let's go back to Gary. Since Gary is big and red, he is round (rule 12). If he were quiet, he would be smart (rule 9). But being smart and big would make him white (rule 8), which contradicts his red color. Therefore, Gary cannot be quiet. So the statement \"Gary is quiet\" is false.\n\nThe correct option is: B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B) False.",
