messages:  [['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is cold. Anne is white. Bob is nice. Bob is white. Dave is blue. Gary is blue. Gary is smart. All blue people are smart. If someone is smart then they are cold. If someone is white then they are quiet. If someone is nice and quiet then they are blue. All white, furry people are blue. If Gary is furry then Gary is cold. If Bob is not white then Bob is smart. All cold, blue people are not furry.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Bob is not blue.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '.\n\nThe correct option is: B) False.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**.\n\n1.**Bob\'s Attributes:**.\n   - Bob is white (Fact 4).\n   - Being white makes Bob quiet (Fact 10).\n   - Bob is nice (Fact 3).\n\n2.**Ignoring the Rule:**.\n   - Since Bob is neither nice nor quiet, Fact 11 does not apply: "If someone is nice and quiet, then they are blue." Therefore, Bob is not blue.\n\n3.**Conclusion:**.\n   - The statement "Bob is not blue" is true because Bob is not blue.']]
