een, she's big. So if Anne is green, she's big, and then by fact 15, she's round. But we don't know if Anne is green yet.\n\nFact 16: If someone is quiet and smart, they are round. Erin is smart, so if she's quiet, she would be round. But we don't know if she's quiet.\n\nLet me try to connect these. Since Erin is smart (fact 5), and smart people are nice (fact 13), she's nice. Now, let's see if being nice tells us anything else. Anne is nice and furry, Harry is nice and furry, but Dave is not nice and is furry. So being nice doesn't necessarily mean being furry, but in the cases given, the nice people are furry except for Erin, but we don't know yet.\n\nWait, no, Erin is nice, but we don't know if she's furry. So let's see if we can find any contradictions or confirmations about Erin being furry.\n\nFrom fact 11: Furry people are green. So if Erin were furry, she would be green. If she's green, from fact 14, she's big. So if Erin is furry, she's green and big.\n\nNow, from fact 12: Big, quiet people are not smart. Erin is smart, so if she were big and quiet, that would be a problem. But if she's big and quiet, she can't be smart, which contradicts fact 5. Therefore, Erin cannot be both big and quiet.\n\nBut if Erin is furry, she's green (fact 11) and thus big (fact 14). So Erin would be big. Now, if she's big, and if she's quiet, then she can't be smart. But Erin is smart, so she can't be both big and quiet. Therefore, if Erin is big (which she would be if she's furry), she can't be quiet. So Erin would be big and not quiet.\n\nWait, but let's see if being big and not quiet affects anything else. From fact 16: If someone is quiet and smart, they are round. Erin is smart, but if she's not quiet, then fact 16 doesn't apply to her. So Erin could be round or not, but we don't know yet.\n\nAlternatively, if Erin is not furry, then she's not green (since fact 11 says furry people are green, but it doesn't say non-furry people can't be green). Wait, no, fact 11 says furry 