it the cow.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the rabbit, which is cold (statement 8), visits the cow. If the rabbit visits the cow, then according to statement 14, the cow would see the cat. But does the rabbit visit the cow?\n\nLooking back, the rabbit visits the cat (statement 10), and the cat visits the rabbit (statement 4). There\'s no direct statement that the rabbit visits the cow. However, statement 17 could imply that if the rabbit is visited by someone who sees the cow, then that someone would visit the cow. But the rabbit is visited by the cat (statement 4), and the rabbit sees the cow (statement 9). So, does the cat, who visits the rabbit, also see the cow? If the cat sees the cow, then according to statement 17, the cat would visit the cow. But we don\'t know if the cat sees the cow.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the rabbit, being cold, visits the cow. If the rabbit visits the cow, then statement 14 applies: the cow sees the cat. But does the rabbit visit the cow? The given statements don\'t say that. The rabbit visits the cat (statement 10), and the cat visits the rabbit (statement 4). So, unless the rabbit also visits the cow, statement 14 doesn\'t apply.\n\nWait, but statement 17 says if something visits the rabbit and sees the cow, then it visits the cow. So, if the cat visits the rabbit (statement 4) and if the cat also sees the cow, then the cat would visit the cow. But do we know if the cat sees the cow? The cow sees the rabbit (statement 6), but the cat\'s perspective isn\'t given. So, unless the cat sees the cow, statement 17 doesn\'t apply.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the rabbit, being cold, visits the cow. If the rabbit visits the cow, then statement 14 applies: the cow sees the cat. But does the rabbit visit the cow? The given statements don\'t say that. The rabbit visits the cat (statement 10), and the cat visits the rabbit (statement 4). So, unless the rabbit also visits the cow, statement 14 doesn\'t apply.\n\nWait, but statement 17 could be a loop. If the c