messages:  [['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is young. Charlie is not red. Gary is not blue. Gary is kind. Gary is not rough. Gary is not young. Harry is green. If Gary is green then Gary is not blue. All young people are blue. If Harry is white and Harry is young then Harry is not green. All red people are green. Blue, young people are red. If someone is green then they are white. If someone is blue and white then they are kind. All red people are not rough. If someone is young and not white then they are rough.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Anne is rough.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '.\n\nThe correct option is: B) False.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**.\n\n1.**Anne is young** (given).\n2.**All young people are blue** (rule 9), so Anne is blue.\n3.**Blue, young people are red** (rule 12), so Anne is red.\n4.**No red people are green** (rule 11), so Anne is not green. \n5.**If someone is green, they are not white** (rule 13), so Anne is not white. \n6.**All red people are rough** (rule 15), so Anne is rough.\n\nThus, the statement "Anne is rough" is true']]
