ever, since Charlie is round, and from statement 8, being rough and white makes him quiet, this seems to support that Charlie is quiet.\n\nBut let's check statement 13: If something is round and rough, then it is nice. Charlie is round (from being young and rough) and rough, so he must be nice. Which aligns with statement 2, so that's consistent.\n\nStatement 12: Rough, nice things are cold. Charlie is rough and nice, so he should be cold. But wait, statement 6 says Gary is cold, and statement 7 says Gary is quiet. So, Charlie being cold doesn't directly affect his quietness, but it's another attribute.\n\nWait, does being cold have any relation to being quiet? From the given statements, only statement 8 links rough and white to quiet. So, unless there's a connection between cold and quiet, Charlie's coldness doesn't affect his quietness.\n\nLet me recap Charlie's attributes:\n\n- Nice (statement 2)\n- Rough (statement 3)\n- White (statement 4)\n- Young (from statement 14, since he's rough)\n- Round (from statement 10, since he's young)\n- Cold (from statement 12, since he's rough and nice)\n- Quiet? (From statement 8, since he's rough and white)\n\nSo, according to statement 8, Charlie should be quiet. But let me make sure there's no contradiction.\n\nIs there any statement that says Charlie is not quiet? The only other quiet thing mentioned is Gary (statement 7). There's no direct statement about Charlie's quietness except through the rules.\n\nWait, statement 9: If Charlie is round and quiet, then he is rough. But we already know Charlie is rough, so this doesn't add anything. It's more of a confirmation.\n\nSo, putting it all together, Charlie is rough, white, and round. Therefore, according to statement 8, he should be quiet. There's no information that contradicts this, so the statement \"Charlie is quiet\" should be true.\n\nBut wait, let me double-check. Is there any possibility that Charlie isn't quiet? The only way that could happen is if being rough and white doesn't necessarily make you quiet, but statement 8 says it does. So unless there's an exception, Charlie should be quiet.\n\nI think I've covered all the connections. So, the answer should be true.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
