final_output:  ["Okay, so I need to figure out if Gary is cold based on the given information. Let me start by listing out all the facts and rules provided.\n\nFirst, let's list the facts about each person:\n\n- Bob is big, cold, furry, and smart.\n- Fiona is cold, not green, and white.\n- Gary is smart.\n- Harry is big, cold, and smart.\n\nNow, the rules:\n\n1. All green people are furry.\n2. If Gary is furry and not smart, then he's white.\n3. Smart people are green.\n4. If Bob is not green and not white, then he's furry.\n5. Big people are cold.\n6. If someone is smart and furry, then they are big.\n7. If someone is white and not cold, then they are not blue.\n8. All cold people are not blue.\n\nWait, but the question is about Gary being cold. Let's focus on Gary.\n\nFrom the facts, Gary is smart. Rule 3 says smart people are green. So Gary is green.\n\nRule 1 says all green people are furry. So Gary is furry.\n\nNow, looking at rule 6: If someone is smart and furry, then they are big. Gary is both smart and furry, so he must be big.\n\nRule 5 says big people are cold. Since Gary is big, he must be cold.\n\nSo, putting it all together: Gary is smart → green → furry → big → cold.\n\nTherefore, Gary is cold. The statement is true.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A", '']
