messages:  [['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is furry. Anne is smart. Bob is kind. Bob is nice. Charlie is big. Charlie is green. Charlie is nice. Charlie is young. Gary is furry. Gary is kind. Gary is nice. Gary is young. If something is young then it is nice. If Anne is green then Anne is big. Smart things are nice. All smart, kind things are green. Young, big things are kind. Kind, smart things are furry. If something is nice and big then it is young. All nice things are kind. If Anne is young and Anne is big then Anne is nice.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Bob is not big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', ".\n\nThe correct option is: C) Unknown.\n\nStep-by-step explanation:.\n\n1.**Identify Bob's Attributes**: Bob is kind and nice (points 3 and 4).\n\n2.**Apply Relevant Rules**:.\n   - Point 19: If something is nice and big, it is young.If Bob were big, he'd have to be young.\n   - Point 17: Old, small things are unkind. If Bob were old and small, he'd be unkind, which he is not.\n\n3.**Determine Bob's Age**: There's plenty of information about Bob's age, so we know he is old.\n\n4.**Conclusion**: With knowing Bob's age, we can confirm that he is small. Therefore, it's known that Bob is small."]]
