      "index": 0,
      "text": " Okay, so I need to figure out whether the statement \"Harry is not white\" is true, false, or unknown based on the given information. Let me start by listing out all the information provided and see how it connects.\n\nFirst, let's list out all the facts:\n\n1. Anne is white.\n2. Erin is round.\n3. Erin is white.\n4. Gary is cold.\n5. Gary is round.\n6. Harry is furry.\n7. Harry is green.\n8. Furry, white people are green.\n9. Nice people are round.\n10. All round, furry people are green.\n11. All cold people are white.\n12. All cold, rough people are round.\n13. All white people are cold.\n14. If someone is cold, then they are furry.\n15. All furry, green people are rough.\n16. All round, green people are cold.\n\nNow, the question is about Harry. From the facts, we know Harry is furry (fact 6) and green (fact 7). So, Harry is both furry and green.\n\nLooking at fact 8: Furry, white people are green. So, if someone is furry and white, they must be green. But Harry is already green, so does that mean he's white? Not necessarily, because fact 8 only tells us about furry and white people, but Harry could be green without being white if he's furry and something else.\n\nWait, fact 15 says all furry, green people are rough. So, since Harry is furry and green, he must be rough. So, Harry is rough.\n\nNow, fact 12: All cold, rough people are round. So, if someone is cold and rough, they are round. But we don't know if Harry is cold yet.\n\nFact 11: All cold people are white. So, if someone is cold, they are white. Fact 13: All white people are cold. So, being white and being cold are equivalent here. So, if someone is white, they are cold, and if someone is cold, they are white.\n\nFact 14: If someone is cold, then they are furry. So, cold implies furry. But Harry is already furry, so that doesn't add new info.\n\nFact 10: All round, furry people are green. Harry is green and furry, but we don't know if he's round.\n\nFact 9: Nice people are round. Not sur