hite and cold are equivalent.\n\nBut from fact 8: Furry, white people are green. Harry is furry and green, so if he\'s white, that fits. But if he\'s not white, then fact 8 doesn\'t apply, but he\'s still green because he\'s furry and green.\n\nWait, but fact 8 says that if someone is furry and white, then they are green. It doesn\'t say that all green people are furry and white. So, Harry could be green without being white, as long as he\'s furry. But he is furry, so that\'s covered.\n\nBut then, from fact 15: All furry, green people are rough. So, Harry is rough.\n\nFrom fact 12: All cold, rough people are round. So, if Harry is cold and rough, he\'s round. But we don\'t know if he\'s cold.\n\nAlternatively, if Harry is round, then from fact 16, since he\'s green and round, he\'s cold. So, if he\'s round, he\'s cold.\n\nBut we don\'t know if he\'s round. So, is there any way to determine if Harry is round?\n\nLooking back, the only people mentioned as round are Erin and Gary. Erin is round and white. Gary is round and cold. So, Erin is round, white, and from fact 11, since she\'s white, she\'s cold. But wait, fact 11 says all cold people are white, but Erin is white, so she must be cold. But in the given facts, Erin is round and white, but not necessarily cold. Wait, no, fact 11 says all cold people are white, but it doesn\'t say all white people are cold. Wait, no, fact 13 says all white people are cold. So, Erin is white, so she must be cold.\n\nWait, but in the given facts, Erin is round and white, but not necessarily cold. But according to fact 13, all white people are cold, so Erin must be cold. So, Erin is cold, round, and white.\n\nGary is cold and round. So, Gary is cold, round, and from fact 11, he\'s white. So, Gary is white, cold, and round.\n\nHarry is furry, green, and rough. So, if Harry is cold, then he\'s white, and if he\'s white, he\'s cold. But we don\'t know if he\'s cold.\n\nWait, but from fact 16: All round, green people are cold. So, if Harr