es him big (point 12). Being big means he's cold (point 11). Being cold means he's furry (point 14). So, yes, Dave is furry.\n\nAlternatively, looking at point 13: furry, round things are big. But we already know Dave is round and big, so that doesn't add new info. Point 16 says all furry, big things are young. But we don't know if Dave is young. The context doesn't mention Dave's age, so that's not relevant here.\n\nSo, putting it all together: Dave is round \u2192 big \u2192 cold \u2192 furry. Therefore, Dave is furry.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A) True\n\nThe reasoning is as follows: Dave is round, which makes him big. Being big means he's cold, and all cold things are furry. Therefore, Dave is furry.\n\nThe correct option is: A",
