messages:  [['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nDave is quiet. Fiona is big. Fiona is furry. Gary is round. Gary is young. Harry is quiet. Harry is rough. If someone is furry then they are rough. Big people are rough. If someone is rough then they are young. If someone is young and round then they are quiet. Big, young people are cold. Cold people are round. If someone is young and not furry then they are not round.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Dave is not big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '.\n\nThe correct option is: A) True.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**.\n\n1.**Given Facts:**.\n   - Dave is quiet.\n   - Fiona is big, furry, rough, and young.\n   - Gary is round and young.\n   - Harry is quiet and rough, hence young.\n   - Rules:.\n     - Furry → Rough.\n     - Big → Rough.\n     - Rough → Young.\n     - Young & Round → Quiet.\n     - Big & Young → Cold.\n     - Cold → Round.\n     - Young & Not Furry → Not Round.\n\n2.**Analyzing Dave:**.\n   - Dave is quiet.Possible reasons:.\n     - He is young and round (from fact 11).\n     - He is small, making him smooth, old, warm, and square (from facts 9, 10, 12, 13), which would also make him loud.\n\n3.**Checking Consistencies:**.\n   - If Dave is small:.\n     - He must be smooth (fact 9) → old (fact 10).\n     - Small & Old → Warm → Square (facts 12, 13).\n     - Old & Square → Loud (fact 11) → inconsistent.\n     - However, from fact 14, Old & Square → Must be Hairless.\n     - Some info states Dave is hairless → consistency.\n\n4.**Conclusion:**.\n   - Dave can be small because that would not require him to be hairless, which is stated.\n   - Therefore, Dave is big']]
