meone is young and cold, then they are red. But it doesn't say that only young, cold people are red. So other people can be red for other reasons. So Dave being red is allowed because point 6 says he is, even though he's not cold.\n\nSo putting it all together, Dave is red according to the given context, and there's no contradiction because the rules allow for redness in other ways beyond just being young and cold. Therefore, the statement \"Dave is red\" is true.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
