16: If the mouse needs the squirrel, then the squirrel likes the mouse. But the mouse's needs aren't specified beyond what's given. The mouse likes the tiger (statement 7) and sees the bald eagle (statement 8). There's no mention of the mouse needing the squirrel or the bald eagle, except statement 3 says the bald eagle needs the mouse.\n\nWait, statement 11 says the squirrel needs the bald eagle. So the squirrel's need is tied to the bald eagle, but the mouse's needs are only mentioned in statement 3 as being needed by the bald eagle.\n\nI don't see any contradictions in the given statements. Statement 3 directly says the bald eagle needs the mouse, and none of the other rules negate that. Therefore, the statement should be true.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
