quiet and nice, so that also makes her furry.\n\nSo, putting it all together:\n\nFiona is nice (given) → Fiona is young (given) → Fiona is kind (because young things are kind) → Fiona is green (because kind things are green) → Fiona is smart (because nice and green things are smart) → Fiona is quiet (because green and smart things are quiet) → Fiona is furry (because quiet things are furry and also because quiet and nice things are furry).\n\nTherefore, Fiona is furry. So the statement is true.\n\nWait, let me double-check if I missed anything. Fiona is nice and young. From young, she\'s kind. From kind, she\'s green. From nice and green, she\'s smart. From green and smart, she\'s quiet. From quiet, she\'s furry. Also, from quiet and nice, she\'s furry. So yes, all paths lead to her being furry.\n\nI don\'t see any contradictions here. So the answer should be True.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A', '']
