\nStatement 10: Red people are kind. Bob is red, so he must be kind. But wait, point 1 says Anne is not kind, but that's about Anne, not Bob. So Bob being red implies he's kind.\n\nStatement 13: Kind people are big. Since Bob is kind (from statement 10), he must be big. Which again aligns with what we deduced earlier.\n\nStatement 12: If someone is kind and green, then they are furry. Bob is kind (from 10), green (from 2), so he must be furry. Which is consistent with point 2.\n\nStatement 4: Gary is not furry. Not relevant to Bob.\n\nStatement 6: All blue people are not round. Erin is not blue (from 3), so this doesn't affect Bob.\n\nStatement 11: If Gary is not blue, then Gary is furry. Gary is not blue (from 4), so he must be furry. But statement 4 says Gary is not furry. Wait, that's a contradiction. Hmm, but maybe I misread.\n\nWait, statement 4 says Gary is not furry. Statement 11 says if Gary is not blue, then he is furry. But Erin is not blue (from 3), but that's about Erin. Wait, no, statement 11 is about Gary. So if Gary is not blue, then he is furry. But statement 4 says Gary is not furry. So if Gary is not blue, he must be furry, but he's not. Therefore, the only way this holds is if Gary is blue. Because if he were not blue, he would have to be furry, which contradicts statement 4. So Gary must be blue. But statement 3 says Erin is not blue, which doesn't affect Gary. So Gary is blue, which makes statement 6 relevant: all blue people are not round. So Gary is blue, so he's not round. But that's about Gary, not Bob.\n\nSo going back to Bob. All the statements about Bob seem consistent. He is round, which makes him big, which makes him green. He's red, so he's kind, which makes him big. All these loop back without contradiction.\n\nWait, but let me check if there's any statement that could make Bob not round. Statement 6 says all blue people are not round. But Bob is red, so he's not blue. So that doesn't affect him. Statement 7: If big and round, then green. Bob is both, so he is green, which is consistent.\n\nIs there any statement that could imply Bob is not round? I don't see any. All the statements about Bob being round are consistent with each other and with the other premises.\n\nSo, based on the given information, Bob is round. Therefore, the statement is true.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
