rel? Or does it mean that someone else (green) eats the squirrel?\n\nI think it's the former because the subject is \"they,\" referring to the someone who is green. So, if the squirrel is green, then the squirrel (they) eats the squirrel. So yes, it's a reflexive action.\n\nAlternatively, maybe it's someone else, but in this context, the squirrel is the only one who is green, so it must be the squirrel itself.\n\nTherefore, the statement is true.\n</think>\n\nThe squirrel is green, so according to the rule, it eats the squirrel, meaning itself. \n\nThe correct option is: A",
