messages:  [['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is cold. Anne is furry. Anne is rough. Anne is smart. Anne is white. Bob is nice. Bob is rough. Erin is cold. Erin is furry. Erin is nice. Erin is rough. Erin is smart. Erin is white. Erin is young. Fiona is cold. Fiona is furry. All smart things are cold. If Bob is young and Bob is cold then Bob is furry. Young things are cold. If Fiona is rough and Fiona is cold then Fiona is smart. Cold, furry things are white. All rough, nice things are young. If something is white and furry then it is smart.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Anne is young.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '.\n\nThe correct option is: C) Unknown.\n\nThe statement "Anne is old" can be confirmed as true or false based on the given information. While Erin and Bob can be inferred to be old due to their attributes and the rules provided, Anne\'s attributes do not meet any conditions that would imply she is old. Therefore, it remains known whether Anne is old.\n']]
