ready have.\n\nFrom statement 16: Big, kind people are nice. Charlie is big and kind, so he must be nice. That's consistent with statement 3.\n\nWait, but let me check if there's any contradiction. Let's see:\n\nHarry is furry (statement 5), so from statement 8, Harry is kind. Harry is nice (statement 6), so from statement 14, since Harry is big? Wait, no, Harry's size isn't mentioned. Wait, Harry is red (statement 7), but that's about color, not size.\n\nWait, but statement 15 says all smart, nice people are red. Anne is smart (statement 1), but is she nice? The context doesn't say. So Anne is smart, so from statement 12, she's furry. From statement 8, she's kind. But does that make her nice? Not necessarily, unless she's big and nice, but we don't know.\n\nBut back to Charlie. Charlie is big, so from statement 9, he's green. From statement 13, he's kind. From statement 16, since he's big and kind, he's nice. So that's consistent with statement 3.\n\nWait, but what about statement 14: All big, nice people are kind. So if Charlie is big and nice, he must be kind, which he is. So no contradiction.\n\nIs there any statement that could make Charlie not nice? Let me see.\n\nWait, statement 15: All smart, nice people are red. So if someone is smart and nice, they must be red. But Charlie's color is green, as per statement 9 and 2. So if Charlie were smart and nice, he would have to be red, but he's green. But Charlie isn't smart; Anne is the smart one. So that doesn't affect Charlie.\n\nWait, but Charlie is big and nice, so from statement 14, he's kind. From statement 16, big and kind people are nice, so that's consistent.\n\nSo all the statements about Charlie being big, green, kind, and nice seem to fit together without any contradictions.\n\nWait, but let me check if Charlie being green affects anything else. From statement 13, green implies kind, which we have. From statement 11, kind and green people are big, which Charlie is.\n\nSo, all the implications seem to support that Charlie is nice. Therefore, the statement \"Charlie is nice\" is true.\n\nWait, but I'm a bit confused because the context directly states that Charlie is nice in statement 3. So unless there's a contradiction elsewhere, it should be true. But I need to make sure that all the other statements don't somehow make Charlie not nice.\n\nWait, another angle: from statement 16, big and kind people are nice. Charlie is big and kind, so he must be nice. So that's another confirmation.\n\nI think I've covered all the relevant statements. So the answer should be true.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
